      "key": [
        "Lowmere",
        "Gull Street",
        "the town"
      ],
      "keysecondary": [],
      "comment": "Lowmere",
      "content": "Lowmere is the last town on the coast road before the map runs out. Slate roofs, one pub (the Drowned Bell), a chapel with no bell, and Gull Street running downhill to the sand. Past the Farlight lighthouse the charts show blank paper and the word UNSURVEYED; locals call that sea the White. Fog comes in off the White in the evenings and the town treats it like weather, not like a ghost story, because they are tired of the ghost story. Things arrive in Lowmere that were lost elsewhere. Nobody here finds this remarkable anymore.",
